      <p>If you are considering a highly seasonal market, make sure the peak season revenue is strong enough to compensate for the slow months. Run your financial projections on a monthly basis rather than just annual averages to ensure you can cover all expenses even during the lowest-performing months. Some seasonal markets are extremely profitable despite their uneven revenue distribution, but you need to plan your finances accordingly.</p>
